[Appica UI](https://appica.dev/ui) components for Rails: rendered with **Phlex 2**, styled with
Appica's **Tailwind v4** classes and made interactive with **Stimulus**. Each component keeps
the compound structure of the React original, so the Appica docs map one to one.

## Components

The pages follow Appica's sidebar categories.

### Actions & Inputs

- [Autocomplete](<%= page_path(:autocomplete) %>): a text input that suggests matching options as you type.
- [Button](<%= page_path(:button) %>): the trigger and action element used across components.

### Overlays

- [Drawer](<%= page_path(:drawer) %>): a panel that slides in from a screen edge, with swipe-to-dismiss and snap points.

## Usage

Include the `UI` kit in any Phlex view and call components like JSX tags:

```ruby
class FrameworkPicker < Phlex::HTML
  include UI

  def view_template
    Autocomplete(items: [ "Next.js", "Remix", "Astro" ]) do
      AutocompleteInput(placeholder: "Search a framework")
      AutocompleteContent do
        AutocompleteEmpty { "No frameworks found." }
        AutocompleteList { |item| AutocompleteItem(value: item) { item } }
      end
    end
  end
end
```

From ERB: `<%%= render FrameworkPicker.new %>`.

## Conventions

- **Render props become blocks.** Appica's `{(item) => …}` render functions are blocks with an
  argument (`AutocompleteList { |item| … }`). Where Appica takes `render={<Button />}`, the part
  yields its attributes: `DrawerTrigger { |trigger| Button(**trigger) { "Open" } }`.
- **`className` is `class:`.** Your classes are merged with the defaults through tailwind_merge,
  so conflicting utilities (`h-14` vs `h-10`) replace them.
- **Events instead of callbacks.** `onValueChange`, `onOpenChange`, … are Stimulus events such as
  `ui--autocomplete:change` and `ui--drawer:open-change`, with the value in `event.detail`.
- **One folder per component.** Ruby parts, the Stimulus controller, CSS and the Lookbook preview
  live together in `app/components/ui/<component>/`.
